{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "0f11509d-c28e-57c5-92c7-239dd2839283",
  "Description": "A net of 196 knots, linked to their neighbours, falls over a sphere.\n\nThe knots are one [RigidBody] on a flat [GridPoints] grid. A [RigidJoint] in Nearby mode links every two knots that start within LinkDistance, which on this grid is each knot's four neighbours.\n\nAKA: cloth, net, fabric, mesh, drape\n\nTips\n- LinkDistance just above the grid spacing links neighbours only; above 1.42 times the spacing it adds the diagonals and the net gets stiffer.\n- CollisionGroup 1 lets the knots pass through each other while they still collide with the sphere.",
